# Qualcomm TEE / SMC Invoke
/dev/smcinvoke    0660    system    drmrpc

# Qualcomm QSEE DMA heaps — stock piano ownership/mode.
# Stock ueventd.rc:93 uses the wildcard for every qcom heap. The single-name
# rule only covered qcom,qseecom and left qcom,qseecom-ta at 0600 root:root,
# so the supplicant (primary gid system, groups 1026/1027/1068) got EACCES
# allocating the TA buffer:
#   QSEECOMPAT: DMA-Buf allocation failed from heap qcom,qseecom-ta errno=13
/dev/dma_heap/qcom,*    0444    system    system

# UFS RPMB and the LUN4 GPT listener, copied verbatim from the stock
# /vendor/etc/ueventd.rc (lines 117-121 of the HyperOS image).
#
# A KeyMint key upgrade has to persist state in RPMB, which is replay-protected
# secure storage reached through qseecomd's RPMB listener. qseecomd drops to uid
# system after registering its listeners, and without these rules the node stays
# root:root, so the listener gets EACCES and every upgrade fails:
#
#   E rpmb_ufs: Unable to open /dev/0:0:0:49476 (error no: 13)
#   E KeyMasterHalDevice: upgrade_key   ret: -8
#   E keystore2: Upgrade failed.
#
# This is a DAC failure, not an SELinux one - no AVC is logged for it, which is
# why it stayed hidden behind the SELinux work for so long.
/dev/0:0:0:49476          0600   system     system
/dev/0:0:0:4              0600   system     root
